Singleton  → one for whole app lifetime
             use for: cache, config, logging
             shared across ALL requests

Scoped     → one per HTTP request
             use for: DbContext, order service
             most services you write = Scoped

Transient  → new every injection
             use for: calculators, validators
             stateless, cheap to create

Captive dependency rule:
Singleton  → can hold Singleton + Transient
Scoped     → can hold Scoped + Transient
NEVER      → Singleton holding Scoped ❌

Interview trigger words:
"stateless"  → Transient
"per request" → Scoped
"shared/cache" → Singleton

